# WinUI XAML language service:
#   - exclude the C# server sources + build output and the test harness/fixtures
#   - the published server (dist/server, produced by `bundle:server`) is NOT excluded and ships in the VSIX
#   - trim debug symbols and XML doc comments
#   - the Native AOT server executables (one per architecture) and the framework-dependent
#     generator host ship without a .NET runtime
server/**
test/**
.vscode-test.mjs
server-test.log
dist/server/**/*.pdb
dist/server/**/*.xml
# Native-linker intermediates. The AOT publish output is clean today, but an SDK or PublishAot
# change that leaves an import library behind would otherwise ship it silently, and native
# artifacts now dominate the VSIX. validate-vsix-server.ps1 rejects these too.
dist/server/**/*.lib
dist/server/**/*.exp
dist/server/**/*.ilk
dist/server/**/*.obj
winapp.yaml
